# XSH pause()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.pause.001
anchor     functions/pause.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       pause() returns after a caught signal (sent 200 ms later) has run
           its handler, with -1 and errno EINTR.
test       t/001-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.pause.002
anchor     functions/pause.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       A process in pause() that gets SIGTERM at SIG_DFL ends by that
           signal; pause() does not return.
nomutant   termination is done by the kernel
test       t/002-terminates.c

assertion  XSH.pause.003
anchor     functions/pause.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       An ignored signal (SIGUSR2 at SIG_IGN, sent first) does not end
           pause(); it returns only after the caught SIGUSR1 sent later.
test       t/003-ignored.c
